     <section class="faq" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" aria-expanded="false">
           <span>Why do cats purr?</span>
           <span class="chevron">⌄</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" hidden>
           <p>
             Cats purr for comfort, communication, and sometimes self-soothing. It often means
             they feel relaxed, but purring can also happen when they are stressed or recovering.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" aria-expanded="false">
           <span>How much sleep do cats need?</span>
           <span class="chevron">⌄</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" hidden>
           <p>
             Most cats sleep around 12 to 16 hours a day, and some kittens or senior cats sleep
             even more. Their bursty hunting instincts make short naps a normal part of the day.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" aria-expanded="false">
           <span>Why do cats knead with their paws?</span>
           <span class="chevron">⌄</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" hidden>
           <p>
             Kneading is a comforting behavior that starts in kittenhood. Adult cats often do it
             when they are content, marking a favorite person or blanket with scent glands in their paws.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" aria-expanded="false">
           <span>Should I feed my cat wet or dry food?</span>
           <span class="chevron">⌄</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" hidden>
           <p>
             Many cats do well with a mix of both. Wet food helps with hydration, while dry food can be
             convenient. The best choice depends on your cat's age, health, and preferences.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>
     </section>
   </main>

   <script>
     const examples = document.querySelectorAll(".example");

     examples.forEach((example) => {
       const button = example.querySelector(".question");
       const details = example.querySelector(".details");

       button.addEventListener("click", () => {
         const isOpen = example.classList.toggle("open");
         button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(isOpen));
         details.hidden = !isOpen;

         if (isOpen) {
           details.style.maxHeight = `${details.scrollHeight}px`;
         } else {
           details.style.maxHeight = "0px";
         }
       });
     });
   </script>
